# fixedbugs, defect 582, lane b19-pack, 2026-10-10, a shape beside the
# packing: a header's `#pragma clang section text=...` placed the program's
# own functions in the header's section, and on this Mac `ld` said of it
# *have unwind information, but it's not a code section*, a raw warning on
# a correct program. The close sets every section back to the target's own
# (`emit/header_state.hero`).

use fixedbugs582/pair

extern "fixedbugs-582-a-header-s-clang-section-leaves-the-program-s-functions-in-their-own.h"
    function llabs(x: i64) -> i64

function main()
    print(pair.second(pair.make(llabs(-42))))
